      <p>A scientist doesn't just <em>use</em> a microscope — the microscope becomes a partner in perception, has agency in what gets seen.</p>
      <p>For AI: it's an actor in the cognitive network. It participates in the generation — responds, suggests directions, constrains possibilities, opens others.</p>
      <p>Morrisville move: <strong>AI isn't a tool the student picks up and puts down. It's a participant in cognition. That's why it matters pedagogically — not because it's powerful, but because it's agentive.</strong></p>
