        <li><strong>Radio/Broadcasting:</strong> augment projection of voice</li>
        <li><strong>Film/Camera:</strong> augment vision (capture/replay)</li>
        <li><strong>Computing:</strong> augments storage AND processing — but generation remains human. Partial.</li>
        <li><strong>AI:</strong> First technology that augments <em>generation itself</em> — the production of new thought</li>
      </ul>
      <p>McLuhan, Ong, Vygotsky, Engelbart, Crawford, Latour, Turkle as theoretical frame.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>AI is the first fully transformative information technology — others were additive <span class="ts">8:29</span></summary>
    <div class="exchange">
      <p>Writing, printing, telegraph, telephone — <strong>additive or marginal</strong>. They extended reach, changed distribution, altered speed. They didn't fundamentally transform what reading, thinking, and writing <em>are</em>.</p>
      <p>AI is first that's <strong>fully transformative</strong> because it participates <em>in the cognition itself</em>. Not infrastructure around thinking — infrastructure <em>within</em> thinking.</p>
